# Data source: 'csv' (bundled replay) or 'http' (real backend in server/).
# The CSV replay is the fallback demo — it needs no backend running.
VITE_DATA_SOURCE=http

# Base URL for the backend API. Every endpoint hangs off this path.
#
# Local dev: leave as /api. vite.config.ts proxies /api -> localhost:8787,
# so there is no CORS setup and nothing to change between machines.
# (The backend's own default port is 8787 — see server/.env.example.)
#
# Production (Vercel): set this to https://<render-service>.onrender.com/api.
# NOTE: Vite inlines this at BUILD time, not runtime — it must be set in the
# Vercel project settings BEFORE the build, and changing it needs a redeploy.
# The backend must also list the Vercel domain in its CORS_ORIGIN.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api
